cff-version: "1.2.0"
message: "If you use this work, please cite the article below."

title: "Referential Regimes: Transformation-Based Identity Profiles for Neutral Substrates"
version: "v0.6.0"
date-released: "2026-10-27"

authors:
  - family-names: Case
    given-names: Denise M.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6165-7389"
    affiliation: "Northwest Missouri State University, School of Computer Science and Information Systems, Maryville, MO, USA"

repository-code: "https://github.com/structural-explainability/paper-200-identity-regimes"
license: "CC-BY-4.0"

abstract: >-
  This repository contains the source materials for Referential Regimes:
  Transformation-Based Identity Profiles for Neutral Substrates. The paper
  investigates identity preservation under transformation using declared
  identity invariants, admissible transformation steps, and explicit effect
  models. Candidate identity profiles and transformation families are kept
  as a stipulated comparison catalog, and selected classification cells are
  derived from the models and certified in Lean 4 for scope decomposition,
  rule refinement, and forking. The results expose dependencies on field
  granularity, transformation semantics, and explicit continuity warrants.
  The paper also establishes conditions for equality and separation of
  identity relations generated by invariant-preserving steps. The results
  are conditional on the declared bases, effect models, and warrants.

